  "question": {
    "text": "<strong>Paragraph:</strong>\nThe figure shows a surface $X Y$ separating two transparent media, medium-1 and medium-2. The lines $a b$ and $c d$ represent wavefronts of a light wave travelling in medium-1 and incident on $X Y$. The lines ef and $g h$ represent wavefronts of the light wave in medium-2 after refraction.<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/tm_QoNKNACdV0vkT1URUx9Z9uiV2_apI_Zxl1TkT2TA.original.fullsize.png\"><br><strong>Question:</strong>\nThe phases of the light wave at $c, d, e$ and $f$ are $\\phi_c, \\phi_d, \\phi_e$ and $\\phi_f$, respectively. It is given that $\\phi_c \\neq \\phi_f$.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "r8rSV",
      "text": "\n$\\phi_c$ cannot be equal to $\\phi_d$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EgDue",
      "text": "\n$\\phi_d$ can be equal to $\\phi_e$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "k4keS",
      "text": "\n$\\left(\\phi_d-\\phi_f\\right)$ is equal to $\\left(\\phi_c-\\phi_e\\right)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "4rEns",
      "text": "\n$\\left(\\phi_d-\\phi_c\\right)$ is not equal to $\\left(\\phi_f-\\phi_e\\right)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "All points on a wavefront are at the same phase.\n$$\n\\begin{array}{rlrl}\n\\therefore & \\phi_d & =\\phi_c \\text { and } \\phi_f=\\phi_e \\\\\n& \\therefore & \\phi_d-\\phi_f & =\\phi_c-\\phi_e\n\\end{array}\n$$\nHence, the correct option is (c).",
    "image": null
  },
